# Build output
out
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Dependencies
node_modules

# VS Code extension testing & packaging
.vscode-test/
*.vsix

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Project-private assets & notes
process

# Claude Code
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/workflows/
.claude/agents/state/

# Large local media (screen-recording tests — not shipped)
assets/*.mov

# Icon design master — the full-resolution source the shipped icon is cropped from.
assets/extension-icon-original.png

# GitHub social-preview card — uploaded via the repo's Settings UI, not served from the tree; kept local.
assets/social-preview.png

# Design library & QA corpus — kept locally, not tracked in the repo.
# Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored entry also matches nested directories — an
# unanchored `docs/` once silently swallowed new fixtures under `src/test/fixtures/docs/`
# (already-tracked files were unaffected, so the breakage only showed up on a fresh clone).
/import-statement-design/
/qa/

# Launch/marketing playbook — post drafts and demo scripts, kept locally, never shipped.
/launch/

# Playwright MCP screenshot/console output (tooling artifact)
.playwright-mcp/

# ExTester screenshots/artifacts if a stale in-repo storage dir ever reappears. The real storage
# (downloaded VS Code/ChromeDriver, isolated profile, staged UI workspace, failure screenshots)
# lives at /tmp/auto-import-extester — a short path, because an in-repo storage dir pushes the
# Extension Host's unix-socket path past macOS's ~104-char limit (see .vscode-test.mjs).
.extester/
